WEBVTT

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:11.990
Please don't expect too much from it.
This story is a simple illustration of the three
Minami sisters and the ordinary life they lead.

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:13.360
Haruka!

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:14.490
Let's have lunch.

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:17.120
Sorry. I didn't bring any today.

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:19.040
Are you buying yours?

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:20.580
You'd better get to the store early if so.

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:23.790
You two should just start without me.

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:25.330
Do you want anything to drink?

00:00:25.330 --> 00:00:26.790
Hm, let's see...

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:28.250
Milk tea!

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:31.010
I'll have a latte, then.

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:33.550
Milk tea and a latte. All right.

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:34.880
Thanks a bunch.

00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:36.390
All right.

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:38.100
Death!

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:40.890
That hurt, Hayami.

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:43.940
Hosaka, what do you think you're doing?

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:44.770
Isn't it obvious?

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:48.860
Today, I will give this homemade lunch to Minami Haruka.

00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:49.730
Death!
Today, I will give this homemade lunch to Minami Haruka.

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:49.900
Today, I will give this homemade lunch to Minami Haruka.

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:51.280
I told you that hurt.

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:53.700
What do you <i>want</i> to do?

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:55.200
Isn't it obvious?

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:58.700
I want Minami Haruka to
.eat my homemade lunch.

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:00.290
Now give it back.

00:01:00.290 --> 00:01:01.830
I feel sorry for you, Hosaka.

00:01:01.830 --> 00:01:05.580
Did you have so much fun cooking that you forgot what you were really after?

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:06.420
What do you mean?

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:09.420
Don't open that lunch box.

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:10.840
Try to remember.

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:13.590
What do you <i>really</i> want
to tell Haruka-chan?

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:17.050
What do I really want to tell her?

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:24.140
You're drenched!

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:27.400
You'll catch a cold if I don't
wipe your sweat away soon.

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:28.860
Worry not.

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:30.110
I'll keep sweating!

00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:38.030
That's right.

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:41.580
I wanted to tell Minami Haruka to wipe away my sweat after club every day!

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:42.790
Right.

00:01:42.790 --> 00:01:47.290
And for that to happen, we need Haruka-chan to join the Girls' Volleyball Club.

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:49.080
Isn't that right, Hosaka?

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:51.420
<i>This</i> is what you really need.

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:57.090
I thank you, Hayami.

00:01:57.630 --> 00:01:58.680
Minami Haruka!

00:01:59.390 --> 00:02:00.890
Join the volleyball club!

00:02:00.890 --> 00:02:02.640
Ew. Hosaka-senpai.

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:06.430
Haruka went to the store
to buy some bread.

00:02:06.430 --> 00:02:07.810
What?

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:11.110
Bread alone does not
make a balanced diet!

00:02:11.110 --> 00:02:13.520
Minami Haruka should know
.that more than anyone.

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:18.570
No, she just forgot to put
.the rice on this morning.

00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:20.660
I understand.

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:23.160
Minami Haruka is more than just a busy high school student.

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:25.580
She also has two lovely
daughters she must look after.

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:29.170
It must indeed be difficult to
.raise children and study.

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:32.340
They're... not her daughters.
They're her sisters.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:37.840
That's why I must support her with my cooking! With my lunch!

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:39.930
U-Um...

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:42.470
I don't think you needed
.to go shirtless for that.

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:44.810
Just you wait, Minami Haruka!

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:48.770
I'll make you the best
.lunch you've ever tasted.

00:02:48.770 --> 00:02:49.690
I promise you.

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:50.980
Listen to me...

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:51.020
I promise you!
Listen to me...

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:52.310
I promise you!

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:54.020
Disgusting.

00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:27.950
The Man Sweats Under the Blue Summer Sky

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:35.540
Natsuki.

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:38.460
Oh, Hosaka-senpai.

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:39.300
'Sup.

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:41.210
You're not coming to practice today?

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:45.550
I'm sorry. I need to prepare dinner for my family.

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:46.390
I see.

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:48.350
Then so be it.

00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:49.140
Yes.

00:04:50.850 --> 00:04:51.640
Wait.

00:04:52.180 --> 00:04:53.230
How many?

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:55.900
How many family members do you have?

00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:57.400
Four.

00:04:57.400 --> 00:04:58.190
I see.

00:04:58.190 --> 00:04:58.860
Understood.

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:00.530
Okay.

00:05:00.530 --> 00:05:01.860
Excuse me.

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:06.570
Natsuki.

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:11.410
You said you couldn't come to practice because you had to prepare dinner for your family,

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:13.370
didn't you?

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:14.080
Yes.

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:16.670
So, that led me to think:

00:05:16.670 --> 00:05:20.130
If I were to make dinner for your family,

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:22.210
you'd be able to focus on practice.

00:05:23.970 --> 00:05:26.050
I have already prepared it for you.

00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:28.050
I packed it in a lunch box.

00:05:29.720 --> 00:05:33.560
It is the rainy season. We must take great care to guard against food poisoning.

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:36.440
I have not forgotten that.

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:39.440
It's a special lunch with
.plenty of royal ginger.

00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:42.190
Don't worry.

00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:45.240
Any volleyball coach
.would do the same.

00:05:45.950 --> 00:05:47.200
Go ahead and take it.

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:48.200
Don't hesitate.

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:50.580
Hosaka-senpai, I can't.

00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:52.490
Why not? Tell me.

00:05:52.490 --> 00:05:57.460
If I were to accept that, someone else may misunderstand badly.

00:05:57.460 --> 00:05:59.170
What do you mean by
"misunderstand badly"?

00:05:59.170 --> 00:05:59.830
Tell me.

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:01.710
I cannot.

00:06:03.340 --> 00:06:04.460
I see.

00:06:05.050 --> 00:06:07.880
I won't question you any further.

00:06:08.970 --> 00:06:10.340
Oh, right.

00:06:10.340 --> 00:06:15.180
I want my family to eat a hot meal,
.so I will go home and cook it myself.

00:06:16.270 --> 00:06:17.770
A hot meal,

00:06:18.310 --> 00:06:20.310
eaten happily together at the table...

00:06:20.940 --> 00:06:23.320
The perfect example of a family.

00:06:24.860 --> 00:06:25.650
Okay.

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:27.360
By the way,

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:28.820
what was that "Oh, right" about?

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:30.160
Did something come to mind?

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:32.070
Nothing at all.

00:06:32.580 --> 00:06:33.700
I see.

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:36.160
Well, I have no intention of
.prying into your family matters.

00:06:36.950 --> 00:06:38.660
But if you should ever
.need my help, just ask.

00:06:39.170 --> 00:06:39.920
I will.

00:06:40.290 --> 00:06:41.710
Now, if you'll excuse me.

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:48.880
I see.

00:06:51.390 --> 00:06:55.470
It would be a lot easier if
.other people would cook.

00:07:03.190 --> 00:07:05.020
What on Earth am I thinking?

00:07:06.230 --> 00:07:08.240
Natsuki's eyes...

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:12.280
He looks like he wants someone adult-like to cook for him.

00:07:13.030 --> 00:07:16.160
What? An adult way to cook food?

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:18.410
No.

00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:23.210
A way to become more like an adult <i>and</i> a way to cook better food.

00:07:23.210 --> 00:07:24.710
Don't mix them up.

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:26.420
Also, I wasn't asking <i>you</i>.

00:07:27.050 --> 00:07:29.840
I know an adult way to cook food.

00:07:31.590 --> 00:07:33.260
Please tell me.

00:07:33.260 --> 00:07:34.350
Sure.

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:35.930
Wear nothing but an apron.

00:07:37.310 --> 00:07:39.850
Are you a genius or just a pervert?

00:07:39.850 --> 00:07:43.480
I hold within this body infinite potential.

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:44.440
Hitomi.

00:07:45.110 --> 00:07:45.730
Yes?

00:07:46.190 --> 00:07:50.030
You might have a hard time
picking up cooking right away,

00:07:50.030 --> 00:07:54.490
but if it's for someone else, you could ask what they like to eat.

00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:55.910
Like to eat...

00:07:55.910 --> 00:07:59.250
For instance, do they like to eat sweet things or salty things?

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:03.170
I don't really know.

00:08:03.670 --> 00:08:05.920
You should start there, then.

00:08:06.460 --> 00:08:07.420
Okay.

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:12.430
But we <i>do</i> know one
.thing that they like.

00:08:12.970 --> 00:08:14.180
Adult nature.

00:08:16.850 --> 00:08:17.720
Good luck.

00:08:17.720 --> 00:08:19.470
Shut up!

00:08:25.060 --> 00:08:26.560
But if you should ever
.need my help, just ask.

00:08:29.780 --> 00:08:30.690
All right.

00:08:30.690 --> 00:08:35.530
I'll ask if he likes sweet or salty foods first.

00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:38.410
Hey, Natsuki.

00:08:38.410 --> 00:08:39.450
All right.

00:08:40.450 --> 00:08:42.080
Those eyes...

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:44.710
He looks like he's resolved to just cook everything by himself!

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:46.920
Oh, what's wrong?

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:48.960
I, uh...

00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:51.550
I love super-sweet things.

00:08:51.550 --> 00:08:52.340
Oh.

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:53.880
I see.

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:01.430
Please, feel free.

00:09:01.430 --> 00:09:05.100
I made this lunch specially for the Girls' Volleyball Team.

00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:15.820
What's wrong, Atsuko?

00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:16.910
Do you feel sick?

00:09:18.030 --> 00:09:21.040
It's better than anything I can make...

00:09:28.210 --> 00:09:31.050
I wonder when this rain's gonna let up.

00:09:31.050 --> 00:09:33.510
Yeah. How many days has it been?

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:38.640
I wonder how many times Uchida's said, "I wonder when this rain's gonna let up."

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:41.260
Yeah, same here.

00:09:41.260 --> 00:09:43.390
Uchida, do you hate the rain?

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:46.770
I don't really hate it.

00:09:47.310 --> 00:09:50.690
It's the rainy season. We need
.to enjoy it while it lasts.

00:09:50.690 --> 00:09:52.900
Enjoy it? How?

00:09:57.030 --> 00:09:58.240
What are you doing?!

00:09:58.240 --> 00:10:00.450
I'm drenched!

00:10:00.450 --> 00:10:01.990
See? Wasn't that fun?

00:10:05.370 --> 00:10:06.580
Stand still!

00:10:06.580 --> 00:10:07.960
No way!

00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:10.130
Hey!

00:10:10.130 --> 00:10:11.960
C'mon, Uchida.

00:10:11.960 --> 00:10:13.750
Hey, give it a break.

00:10:14.050 --> 00:10:15.880
Catch me if you can!

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:17.340
You little!

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:27.270
Yoshino, I'm sorry.

00:10:27.270 --> 00:10:28.770
Wow, I'm soaked.

00:10:28.770 --> 00:10:31.520
Apologize to me too!

00:10:33.150 --> 00:10:34.940
What happened?

00:10:34.940 --> 00:10:36.490
You're all soaking wet.

00:10:36.490 --> 00:10:38.070
It's all Touma's fault!

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:39.200
No, it's Uchida's!

00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:41.570
It's both your faults!

00:10:41.570 --> 00:10:44.450
You were splashing too by the end, Chiaki.

00:10:44.450 --> 00:10:47.000
Just get in the bath.

00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:48.210
Okay.

00:10:51.380 --> 00:10:52.630
Sheesh,

00:10:52.630 --> 00:10:55.880
all because you had to keep
.going on about the rain.

00:10:55.880 --> 00:10:58.510
It's because you kicked water at me!

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:01.180
And after everyone splashed each other,

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:04.050
Chiaki splashed back using
.her umbrella like a golf club.

00:11:04.050 --> 00:11:07.520
Once you get splashed, it doesn't
.matter how much wetter you get.

00:11:07.980 --> 00:11:10.390
Wait, Haruka, what did you say?

00:11:10.770 --> 00:11:13.110
It's been raining for days now.

00:11:13.110 --> 00:11:15.520
Our laundry just isn't drying.

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:18.030
And Chiaki doesn't have enough spares.

00:11:18.610 --> 00:11:22.410
So you want to give
them <i>my</i> clothes to wear?

00:11:22.410 --> 00:11:23.490
I see.

00:11:24.580 --> 00:11:25.410
And I refuse!

00:11:26.450 --> 00:11:27.580
What's wrong?

00:11:27.580 --> 00:11:29.660
If I do that, I'll have
.nothing left to wear.

00:11:30.960 --> 00:11:33.040
I'm sure something else of
.yours will dry tomorrow.

00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:36.710
How do you know that? Why not lend them <i>your</i> clothes?

00:11:37.090 --> 00:11:39.380
Because mine are too big
for them! It'd look weird!

00:11:39.380 --> 00:11:40.970
But maybe it wouldn't!

00:11:44.350 --> 00:11:46.140
What's wrong, Chiaki?

00:11:46.140 --> 00:11:48.270
Don't worry. It's nothing important.

00:11:48.270 --> 00:11:52.980
When you say something's not important, it usually ends up being really important.

00:11:52.980 --> 00:11:54.150
Really?

00:11:54.150 --> 00:11:55.980
So what's wrong?

00:11:56.360 --> 00:12:00.490
Well, we put all our towels in the wash, and I don't think they're dry yet.

00:12:02.450 --> 00:12:04.240
Then how are we
going to dry ourselves?

00:12:05.320 --> 00:12:07.790
Why can't they just change
back into their uniforms?

00:12:08.330 --> 00:12:10.660
They won't be dry in time.

00:12:10.660 --> 00:12:12.290
Besides, they don't have any underwear.

00:12:14.290 --> 00:12:15.750
Why don't you lend them yours?

00:12:15.750 --> 00:12:18.210
Mine are too big for them.

00:12:18.210 --> 00:12:19.960
That's true.

00:12:20.590 --> 00:12:22.050
What now?

00:12:22.380 --> 00:12:25.260
I don't think the towels
..are done drying yet...

00:12:25.260 --> 00:12:27.050
Then how are they
going to dry themselves?

00:12:30.350 --> 00:12:31.560
Nothing there.

00:12:31.560 --> 00:12:32.890
Nothing.

00:12:32.890 --> 00:12:34.520
I figured.

00:12:35.520 --> 00:12:38.320
All right. Then until we have
something to dry ourselves...

00:12:38.770 --> 00:12:40.070
Let's have fun in the bath!

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:43.280
Take that!

00:12:43.280 --> 00:12:45.660
Stop that! It's dangerous!

00:12:45.660 --> 00:12:46.820
You've done it now!

00:12:46.820 --> 00:12:48.120
Take that!

00:12:48.120 --> 00:12:49.450
Missed me by a mile!

00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:50.040
I'm gonna get you!

00:12:50.910 --> 00:12:53.660
All we have left are hand towels.

00:12:53.660 --> 00:12:56.040
I'll have to wash them again...

00:12:58.040 --> 00:13:00.800
They'll be dry in a bit, so just wait.

00:13:01.130 --> 00:13:03.260
We are truly grateful, Haruka-chan.

00:13:03.260 --> 00:13:04.430
Yes, truly grateful.

00:13:04.430 --> 00:13:05.050
I'm honored.

00:13:06.510 --> 00:13:09.930
If I'd known this'd happen,
I would've made different clothes.

00:13:12.680 --> 00:13:13.890
All right!

00:13:13.890 --> 00:13:15.520
Uchida, let's wrestle!

00:13:15.520 --> 00:13:16.770
Why?!

00:13:17.150 --> 00:13:19.230
Because it's fun!

00:13:19.770 --> 00:13:20.440
Watch out!

00:13:24.780 --> 00:13:27.450
Let's just quietly wait until it dries.

00:13:27.450 --> 00:13:28.700
Sure.

00:13:29.280 --> 00:13:30.580
All right, done.

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:34.330
Hey, what's with this?

00:13:34.330 --> 00:13:35.460
Chiaki-sama,

00:13:35.460 --> 00:13:39.340
we ask that you make the rain clouds go away.

00:13:39.340 --> 00:13:42.840
I wish the clear, blue sky would come back.

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:44.670
Chiaki, you can do it.

00:13:45.670 --> 00:13:48.340
I'm playing soccer with Fujioka tomorrow.

00:13:48.340 --> 00:13:50.100
Stop wishing and praying to me!

00:13:50.640 --> 00:13:52.180
Haruka-neesama!

00:13:52.180 --> 00:13:54.060
Can you tell these three to stop—?

00:13:54.060 --> 00:13:55.560
Please, Chiaki.

00:13:55.560 --> 00:13:56.640
At this rate,

00:13:56.640 --> 00:13:58.980
we won't have any clothes to wear tomorrow.

00:13:59.400 --> 00:14:01.110
Haruka-neesama...

00:14:01.110 --> 00:14:02.900
You too?

00:14:13.740 --> 00:14:16.120
I made sunny-side up eggs today.

00:14:16.120 --> 00:14:17.580
But they weren't that good.

00:14:17.580 --> 00:14:19.040
In what way?

00:14:19.040 --> 00:14:21.290
It was kinda like...

00:14:21.290 --> 00:14:25.880
They were still pretty raw.
Like, not even half-done.

00:14:25.880 --> 00:14:28.090
Maybe you're taking them
off the heat too quick.

00:14:28.510 --> 00:14:31.180
Personally, I like my eggs nicely browned.

00:14:31.180 --> 00:14:33.930
Though I feel like I'm the
one turning brown right now.

00:14:33.930 --> 00:14:34.930
Huh?

00:14:35.680 --> 00:14:38.440
Guess you're right. It's been a while since it's been this sunny.

00:14:38.940 --> 00:14:40.900
Sure feels like summer.

00:14:40.900 --> 00:14:41.940
Right?

00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:45.440
I can't say I don't like not browning either.

00:14:46.070 --> 00:14:50.030
You mean eggs? Or tanning?

00:14:50.360 --> 00:14:53.530
I wonder which it is.

00:14:53.530 --> 00:14:56.290
What about you, Haruka-chan?
Do you like them nicely browned?

00:14:57.250 --> 00:14:58.870
Well...

00:14:58.870 --> 00:15:00.420
I can't say I don't like them.

00:15:00.420 --> 00:15:02.040
I see.

00:15:02.040 --> 00:15:05.050
So you don't hate them nicely browned.

00:15:05.550 --> 00:15:06.960
What's she talking about?

00:15:06.960 --> 00:15:08.170
I wonder.

00:15:08.170 --> 00:15:12.720
But people have different preferences as to how cooked they want their eggs.

00:15:12.720 --> 00:15:14.680
Yeah.

00:15:15.850 --> 00:15:17.850
Preferences, huh?

00:15:21.190 --> 00:15:21.940
Hey, hey.

00:15:22.310 --> 00:15:24.730
Hosaka's skin is pretty
pale, don't you think?

00:15:24.730 --> 00:15:26.190
Even though he's in the volleyball club.

00:15:26.190 --> 00:15:28.490
He's got a nice face, but...

00:15:30.570 --> 00:15:32.490
Sunny-side up.

00:15:32.490 --> 00:15:34.030
Turned over.

00:15:34.030 --> 00:15:35.410
Sunny-side up.

00:15:36.080 --> 00:15:37.660
Turned over.

00:15:37.660 --> 00:15:39.370
Sunny-side up.

00:15:39.370 --> 00:15:41.000
Turned over.

00:15:42.920 --> 00:15:44.380
Sunny-side up!

00:15:44.960 --> 00:15:47.000
Something about his brain...

00:15:47.340 --> 00:15:48.920
Turned over!

00:15:48.920 --> 00:15:51.760
Hosaka, I'm sorry to interrupt your external monologue.

00:15:52.380 --> 00:15:57.100
What is it? I'm currently running mental simulations of breakfast eggs for Minami Haruka.

00:15:57.100 --> 00:15:58.770
From what I hear,

00:15:59.520 --> 00:16:00.770
Haruka-chan...

00:16:00.770 --> 00:16:04.190
doesn't mind them nicely browned.

00:16:04.190 --> 00:16:04.940
What?

00:16:04.940 --> 00:16:06.150
Is that so?

00:16:06.980 --> 00:16:09.440
Wait, she doesn't mind <i>what</i> nicely browned?

00:16:09.860 --> 00:16:12.360
I wonder.

00:16:12.360 --> 00:16:15.070
It might be how cooked her eggs are.

00:16:15.070 --> 00:16:17.450
It might be how tanned her men are.

00:16:17.950 --> 00:16:19.500
I see.

00:16:19.500 --> 00:16:20.620
So that's it.

00:16:23.040 --> 00:16:24.120
Hosaka?

00:16:24.120 --> 00:16:25.460
Where are you going?

00:16:27.380 --> 00:16:28.800
Natsuki.

00:16:29.460 --> 00:16:33.800
This might sound random, but how cooked do you like your eggs?

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:35.760
Huh? Why do you ask?

00:16:35.760 --> 00:16:37.800
I'm just curious.

00:16:38.680 --> 00:16:40.470
I prefer them when
.they're not overcooked.

00:16:40.470 --> 00:16:41.480
I see.

00:16:43.270 --> 00:16:47.650
In other words, he likes me
.untanned like I am now.

00:16:47.650 --> 00:16:51.320
No, no, we're just talking about eggs.

00:16:52.240 --> 00:16:54.780
Since she mentioned eggs, I...

00:16:54.780 --> 00:16:56.320
I kind of want...

00:16:57.320 --> 00:17:00.700
Don't look at me with those
"I want to eat you" eyes!

00:17:00.700 --> 00:17:02.330
I want to eat some eggs.

00:17:04.160 --> 00:17:08.250
To fry an egg well, you need to turn it over.

00:17:08.250 --> 00:17:10.000
You need to cook both sides.

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:11.840
Apply an even amount of heat to both sides.

00:17:12.340 --> 00:17:13.800
That's what's most important.

00:17:13.800 --> 00:17:16.430
The timing of the flip.

00:17:18.470 --> 00:17:19.140
It's time.

00:17:22.520 --> 00:17:24.390
Turn over.

00:17:25.270 --> 00:17:27.440
Just you wait, Minami Haruka.

00:17:27.440 --> 00:17:30.730
I will give you the greatest
.turn-over you've ever had.

00:17:36.950 --> 00:17:38.990
Hosaka, what's that?

00:17:38.990 --> 00:17:40.080
Hayami?

00:17:40.780 --> 00:17:45.160
I couldn't find a vessel to hold my
.latest dish for Minami Haruka.

00:17:45.160 --> 00:17:46.870
So I made one myself.

00:17:49.080 --> 00:17:52.840
You made this? It's pretty good.

00:17:52.840 --> 00:17:55.970
Indeed. I finally made one
that I considered acceptable.

00:17:55.970 --> 00:17:58.640
Its color cannot be expressed
with human words—

00:17:58.640 --> 00:17:59.890
It's white.

00:18:02.600 --> 00:18:06.980
Its shape is completely unique, calculated and designed specifically for my cuisine—

00:18:06.980 --> 00:18:08.100
It's circular.

00:18:09.610 --> 00:18:12.150
So what do you plan to fill this with?

00:18:14.530 --> 00:18:17.400
H-Huh? Are you mad?

00:18:17.900 --> 00:18:20.370
Mad? Why would I be mad?

00:18:20.370 --> 00:18:22.740
I am Hosaka, a vessel for tolerance itself!

00:18:24.620 --> 00:18:28.500
Those who behold it may describe its
.shape and color however they wish.

00:18:28.500 --> 00:18:30.500
No need to restrict it to any one use.

00:18:30.920 --> 00:18:35.340
Yes. I must ask others what they
.believe its proper use to be.

00:18:35.340 --> 00:18:39.260
Where are you going, Hosaka?

00:18:43.010 --> 00:18:44.560
I've been waiting.

00:18:46.890 --> 00:18:48.270
Hosaka-senpai?

00:18:49.020 --> 00:18:53.900
You two, what is the most important thing to
consider when preparing the very best cuisine?

00:18:53.900 --> 00:18:56.940
U-Uh, I wonder what...

00:18:56.940 --> 00:18:59.660
Is it... love?

00:18:59.660 --> 00:19:00.660
That's right!

00:19:00.660 --> 00:19:03.580
But no, not in this case.

00:19:04.200 --> 00:19:06.660
The very best cuisine
.requires the very best vessel.

00:19:06.660 --> 00:19:08.210
Oh, that's what you meant.

00:19:08.210 --> 00:19:09.670
I'm sorry I didn't realize.

00:19:09.670 --> 00:19:10.580
Sorry.

00:19:10.960 --> 00:19:13.670
And so, I made the very best vessel.

00:19:15.050 --> 00:19:17.550
You made this, Hosaka-senpai?

00:19:18.300 --> 00:19:19.380
This is...

00:19:19.380 --> 00:19:20.800
Um...

00:19:20.800 --> 00:19:23.300
It looks very impressive.

00:19:23.680 --> 00:19:24.970
Indeed.

00:19:24.970 --> 00:19:27.470
It does indeed look very impressive.

00:19:28.390 --> 00:19:30.890
It took quite some time to complete.

00:19:31.440 --> 00:19:33.060
First, I had to select the clay.

00:19:33.060 --> 00:19:36.440
Of all the clays available to me, I chose kaolin,

00:19:36.730 --> 00:19:37.980
also known as china clay,

00:19:37.980 --> 00:19:41.150
the main material used in Meissen porcelain, the pinnacle of Western china.

00:19:41.150 --> 00:19:45.080
Its unique whiteness, its peculiar whiteness,
.and its pure whiteness are like none other.

00:19:45.080 --> 00:19:48.910
You see, earthenware grants food which rests upon it a certain quality.

00:19:48.910 --> 00:19:51.580
I realized that, in order to understand the properties of the earth

00:19:51.580 --> 00:19:54.330
and bring out this quality, I had to bake my earthenware myself.

00:19:54.330 --> 00:19:58.130
And so, I chose to glaze it with a white enamel, to make that which was white shine an even brighter white.

00:19:58.130 --> 00:19:59.380
I tried, time and time again.

00:19:59.380 --> 00:20:01.680
And this was the final result!

00:20:01.680 --> 00:20:05.890
As bright as the early summer sun, but with a gentle glow like that of the moon, enveloping you in its light.

00:20:05.890 --> 00:20:08.270
That is the delicate color I was able to bring forth.

00:20:08.270 --> 00:20:10.560
If I were to express it in human words, I would call it...

00:20:10.560 --> 00:20:11.640
Silver!

00:20:11.640 --> 00:20:13.560
See how it shines!

00:20:13.560 --> 00:20:15.060
And its shape.

00:20:15.060 --> 00:20:17.980
If the cuisine is a person, then the vessel is his clothes.

00:20:17.980 --> 00:20:19.940
How miserable it would be if the man made the clothes,

00:20:19.940 --> 00:20:22.320
but how foolish it would it be if the clothes made the man!

00:20:22.320 --> 00:20:24.030
The cuisine and its vessel must be equals!

00:20:24.030 --> 00:20:26.410
One must bring out the best in the other!

00:20:26.410 --> 00:20:27.780
Yes, yes, indeed, indeed!

00:20:27.780 --> 00:20:29.370
And thus, I completed it!

00:20:29.370 --> 00:20:32.580
If I were to describe the beauty of the shape which brings out the best in food, I would call it...

00:20:32.580 --> 00:20:34.330
The beauty of form dictated solely by function!

00:20:34.330 --> 00:20:36.460
It is the simplest, and therefore the best!

00:20:36.460 --> 00:20:40.340
And so, what do you two think I should use this vessel for?

00:20:40.340 --> 00:20:41.880
Let's boil water in it!

00:20:42.420 --> 00:20:43.930
I shall follow your suggestion.

00:20:45.890 --> 00:20:48.220
Hosaka, what's that?

00:20:48.220 --> 00:20:49.260
A kettle?

00:20:49.260 --> 00:20:50.850
So you see it as that too?

00:20:52.520 --> 00:20:53.520
Hot water...

00:20:54.190 --> 00:20:58.940
Can I bring Minami Haruka happiness with hot water alone?

00:20:59.940 --> 00:21:02.280
Tell me, O kettle!

00:21:02.740 --> 00:21:05.660
What happened to your plate?

00:21:13.790 --> 00:21:15.870
Kana, count three minutes.

00:21:15.870 --> 00:21:16.790
Sure.

00:21:17.130 --> 00:21:21.880
One, two, three, four, five,

00:21:21.880 --> 00:21:23.670
Yours looks good, Chiaki.
six, seven, eight, nine, ten, eleven...

00:21:23.670 --> 00:21:26.090
Would you like to try a bit when it's done?
six, seven, eight, nine, ten, eleven...

00:21:26.090 --> 00:21:28.220
Then why don't we trade a bite with each other?
six, seven, eight, nine, ten, eleven...

00:21:28.220 --> 00:21:28.510
Then why don't we trade a bite with each other?

00:21:28.510 --> 00:21:30.310
No fair! I wanna too!

00:21:30.310 --> 00:21:31.850
You keep counting.

00:21:31.850 --> 00:21:34.140
Fifteen, sixteen, seventeen, eighteen...

00:21:34.140 --> 00:21:35.940
We can trade too, Kana.
Fifteen, sixteen, seventeen, eighteen...

00:21:35.940 --> 00:21:36.020
Sure.
Fifteen, sixteen, seventeen, eighteen...

00:21:36.020 --> 00:21:36.650
Sure.

00:21:36.650 --> 00:21:38.020
You keep counting.

00:21:38.020 --> 00:21:42.070
Twenty-one, twenty-two, twenty-three, twenty-four, twenty-five,

00:21:42.070 --> 00:21:47.030
twenty-six, twenty-seven, twenty-eight, twenty-nine, three minutes!

00:21:47.030 --> 00:21:48.820
No cheating!

00:23:22.210 --> 00:23:25.550
Chiaki-sama, please tell me how to become more like an adult.

00:23:25.550 --> 00:23:29.840
Do you want to become more adult so you can do weird things?

00:23:29.840 --> 00:23:32.640
Next time: "Making Chilled Noodles."

00:23:32.640 --> 00:23:35.140
How about how to become a better cook?
